{"term":"responsible","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b4623989f87a2473d9","definition":"Having the duty of taking care of something; answerable for an act performed or for its consequences; accountable; amenable, especially legally or politically.","example":"Parents are responsible for their child's behaviour.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"postpositional","register":"postpositional","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d81ca6bd6ff6a8cfa8","definition":"Being a primary cause of a situation or action and thus able to be blamed or credited for it.","example":"Who is responsible for this mess?","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"postpositional","register":"postpositional","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:608c6ae0341d681abe","definition":"Answerable to (a superior).","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:51876fbc241d472204","definition":"Involving important duties; involving a degree of personal accountability on the part of the person concerned.","example":"She has a responsible position in the firm.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7dcee10a7133eb0247","definition":"Having good judgment in decision-making.","example":"But was it responsible governance to pass the Longitude Act without other efforts to protect British seamen? Or might it have been subterfuge—a disingenuous attempt to shift attention away from the realities of their life at sea.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:de01b72e581bf2a63c","definition":"Able to be trusted; reliable; trustworthy.","example":"He looks like a responsible guy.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a28e4730b64272760c","definition":"Capable of rational conduct and thus morally accountable for one's behavior.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["irresponsible"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d2ec46e7617b9d22f0","definition":"The person who bears the responsibility for something.","example":"Were this not so, long since would we have traced directly home the responsibility for the war on Freedom in the Philippines. Long since, would we have hanged the responsibles as traitors to our country.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["co-responsible","eco-responsible","irresponsibility","irresponsible","nonresponsible","responsibility","responsibilize","responsibleness","responsible trading","responsibly","semiresponsible","superresponsible","unresponsible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e